{"name":"Raw Sienna","hex":"#9a6200","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"raw sienna","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A yellowish brown colour."]},{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Of a yellowish brown colour."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/raw_sienna"}],"entries":[{"title":"Sienna","blocks":[{"text":"Sienna is an earth pigment containing iron oxide and manganese oxide. In its natural state, it is yellowish brown, and it is called raw sienna. When heated, it becomes a reddish brown, and it is called burnt sienna. It takes its name from the city-state of Siena, where it was produced during the Renaissance. Along with ochre and umber, it was one of the first pigments to be used by humans, and is found in many cave paintings. Since the Renaissance, it has been one of the brown pigments most widely used by artists."}],"link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Sienna","wikidata":"Q899318"},{"title":"Raw Sienna (album)","blocks":[{"text":"Raw Sienna is the fifth studio album by British blues rock band Savoy Brown. It was recorded and released by Decca in the United Kingdom in 1970 in both mono and stereo. For release in United States and Canada, masters were leased to Parrot Records —PAS 71036."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/b/bc/Raw_Sienna_-_Savoy_Brown.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Raw_Sienna_(album)","wikidata":"Q7296890"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/79/Monteriggioni0001.jpg/120px-Monteriggioni0001.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/79/Monteriggioni0001.jpg/250px-Monteriggioni0001.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/79/Monteriggioni0001.jpg/120px-Monteriggioni0001.j